Solidity <-> Natural Language Alignment Dataset - Licensing
===========================================================

Two layers of rights apply to this dataset.

1. Dataset packaging and natural-language descriptions
   The manifest, metadata, curation scripts, and every generated `<id>.txt`
   description are released under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
   (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Solidity sources (`<id>.sol`)
   Each contract is redistributed under the license of its upstream project.
   The per-sample license is recorded in `data/<id>/meta.json` (`license`) and
   in `index/manifest.jsonl`, together with the upstream repository URL and the
   exact commit in `source.provenance` / `source.version`.

   Licenses present in this corpus include MIT, AGPL-3.0, LGPL-3.0,
   GPL-2.0-or-later, and BUSL-1.1. BUSL-1.1 sources (Uniswap v3 core, Aave v3)
   carry use restrictions until their stated change date; consult the upstream
   repository before any production use.

   Samples in the `verified` split are Etherscan-verified on-chain sources
   mirrored via Smart Contract Sanctuary. Their license is whatever the deployer
   declared in the SPDX header of the deployed source (often none), so they are
   marked `unknown` and are included for research use only.

Attribution for each sample is carried in `meta.json.source.attribution`.
